{
  "id": "u13-l02",
  "unit": "u13-requests",
  "title": "Please come in",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "**আপনি has two command forms, both polite.**\n\n- **Everyday Bangladesh:** the আপনি present form, as in **দেন**, **যান**, **থামেন**: **বসেন** 'sit', **বলেন** 'say'.\n- **Standard (signs, offices, Kolkata):** take the আমি form, drop -ই, add **-উন**: বসি → **বসুন**, বলি → **বলুন**, শুনি → **শুনুন**, আসি → **আসুন**. Like **দিন**, 'take' is **নিন**.\n\n**ভিতরে আসুন, বসুন** 'Come in, have a seat' is what a host says. **শুনুন** 'listen' is also how you politely say 'Excuse me' to a stranger.\n\n**দয়া করে** 'please' is formal or pleading; the polite verb already does most of the work.",
  "vocab": [
    {
      "id": "boshen",
      "bn": "বসেন",
      "tr": "boshen",
      "en": "sit (polite)",
      "notes": "Everyday Bangladeshi polite command; same form as আপনি বসেন 'you sit'. Standard: বসুন."
    },
    {
      "id": "boshun",
      "bn": "বসুন",
      "tr": "boshun",
      "en": "please sit (standard)",
      "notes": "Standard polite command: বসি → বস- + -উন. Everyday Bangladeshi speech often uses বসেন."
    },
    {
      "id": "ashun",
      "bn": "আসুন",
      "tr": "ashun",
      "en": "please come (standard)",
      "notes": "আসি → আস- + -উন. Everyday Bangladeshi speech also uses আসেন."
    },
    {
      "id": "bolun",
      "bn": "বলুন",
      "tr": "bolun",
      "en": "please say (standard)",
      "notes": "বলি → বল- + -উন. Everyday Bangladeshi speech also uses বলেন."
    },
    {
      "id": "shunun",
      "bn": "শুনুন",
      "tr": "shunun",
      "en": "please listen; excuse me",
      "notes": "শুনি → শুন- + -উন. Also the polite way to get a stranger's attention. Everyday Bangladeshi speech also uses শোনেন."
    },
    {
      "id": "nin",
      "bn": "নিন",
      "tr": "nin",
      "en": "please take (standard)",
      "notes": "Irregular, like দিন. Everyday Bangladeshi speech also uses নেন."
    },
    {
      "id": "doya-kore",
      "bn": "দয়া করে",
      "tr": "doya kore",
      "en": "please",
      "notes": "Literally 'doing a kindness'. Formal or pleading; in everyday talk a polite verb form plus একটু is enough."
    }
  ],
